<title>USA: Petroecuador lifts force majeure on Oriente crude.</title>
<headline>Petroecuador lifts force majeure on Oriente crude.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's state oil company Petroecuador lifted its declaration of force majeure on March cargoes of Oriente crude effective Friday, a company official said.</p>
<p>The company declared the measure on March 7 after a pump exploded on the main Transecuadoran pipeline.  </p>
<p>Petroecuador expects to push forward the dates on some eight to 10 cargoes of Oriente by a few days as a result of the accident, the official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The pipeline flow is back to normal,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Operations had been curtailed from March 7 to March 12.</p>
<p>Petroecuador normally exports about 20 Oriente cargoes per month.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
